      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::019::dislocation_mechanisms_for_fcc_to_hcp_ph"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Mn in CrMnFeCoNi introduces magnetic frustration that suppresses the FCC-to-HCP transformation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::008::effect_of_magnetism",
        "PMC5893566::web::019::dislocation_mechanisms_for_fcc_to_hcp_ph"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quinary alloy and all relevant quaternary and ternary derivatives are single-phase FCC after thermomechanical processing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::008::effect_of_magnetism"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloys should be compared using deformation tests at matched temperatures, strain rates, and loading conditions.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The compared alloys should have similar grain sizes and single-phase FCC starting structures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The structural mediator is deformation-induced HCP nanolath formation localized along stacking faults and twin boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::019::dislocation_mechanisms_for_fcc_to_hcp_ph"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local magnetic configurations control the FCC-HCP free-energy difference.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC5893566::web::008::effect_of_magnetism",
        "PMC5893566::web::019::dislocation_mechanisms_for_fcc_to_hcp_ph"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation slip and interactions with internal boundaries trigger the localized FCC-to-HCP transformation in CrCoNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The deformation-induced transformation increases strength while retaining or enhancing ductility in CrCoNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CrMnFeCoNi, CrCoNi will develop a higher density of deformation-induced HCP nanolaths.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
